Ruric Thar taxes noncreature spells six life, and he taxes YOU too. The entire deck is built around that one fact: almost every card here is a creature, so his trigger is close to one-sided. Ramp is mana dorks, removal is creatures that fight, and card draw is creatures that draw. When you do run a noncreature spell it earns its slot, and you cast it before he lands or while you can afford the six.

# The commander
Ruric Thar, the Unbowed :: 6/6 reach and vigilance, must attack every combat, and every noncreature spell any player casts deals six to its caster. In a four-player pod that is twelve to eighteen damage a turn cycle that you did nothing to earn.
Absorbing Man and Titania :: doubles all damage your CREATURE sources deal. Ruric Thar's trigger is a creature source, so every noncreature spell now costs them TWELVE. This is the single biggest upgrade in the deck.
Dragonborn Champion :: draws a card whenever a source you control deals five or more damage to a player. Ruric Thar's six qualifies, so every spell they cast is a card for you.
Rhythm of the Wild :: your creatures cannot be countered and they all get haste or a counter. It is the closest thing to a noncreature spell this deck is happy to cast.

# Stacking the tax
Scytheclaw Raptor :: four damage to anyone casting a spell on someone else's turn. Between this and Ruric Thar, instant-speed interaction costs ten.
Adrenaline Jockey :: the second copy of that effect.
Magebane Lizard :: escalating damage for every noncreature spell in a turn, so combo turns are lethal to their pilot.
Cindervines :: a ping per noncreature spell, and it sacrifices to destroy an artifact or enchantment and burn its controller.
Shadow in the Warp :: two damage on their first noncreature spell each turn, and your first creature each turn costs two less.
Heartwood Storyteller :: every noncreature spell any opponent casts draws each of their opponents a card. In a creature deck you are the player who benefits most.
Combustion Man :: on every attack they either lose a permanent or take four.

# Making your spells uncounterable
Green creature decks lose to counterspells, so the deck simply removes that as an option.
Allosaurus Shepherd :: one mana, and every green spell you control becomes uncounterable.
Frenzied Baloth :: the same for creature spells, plus haste and trample, and combat damage cannot be prevented — so fogs stop working.
Destiny Spinner :: creature and enchantment spells cannot be countered, and it animates a land as a finisher.
Hexing Squelcher :: your spells cannot be countered and your whole board gets ward.
Last March of the Ents :: cannot be countered, draws cards equal to your biggest toughness, and dumps your hand onto the battlefield.

# Ramp, all of it creatures or auras
Birds of Paradise :: turn-one fixing.
Llanowar Elves :: and the green half.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the second copy.
Elvish Mystic :: the third.
Arbor Elf :: untaps a Forest, and with Overgrowth or Fertile Ground on it that is two or three mana.
Overgrowth :: two extra green off one land.
Fertile Ground :: one extra of any colour.
Fanatic of Rhonas :: four green mana once you have a four-power creature, which is immediate in this deck.
Carpet of Flowers :: free mana every turn against any blue deck at the table.
Delighted Halfling :: uncounterable mana for legendary spells, which covers Ruric Thar himself.
Klauth, Unrivaled Ancient :: mana equal to your attacking creatures' total power, every combat. On a real board that is fifteen or more.
Goreclaw, Terror of Qal Sisma :: your big creatures cost two less and get +1/+1 with trample when he attacks.

# Removal without noncreature spells
Silverback Elder :: every creature spell destroys an artifact or enchantment, ramps you, or gains four life. It is the answer to the stax pieces Gruul normally cannot touch.
Kogla, the Titan Ape :: fights on entry and destroys an artifact or enchantment on every attack.
Balefire Dragon :: connects and wipes one player's entire board.
Drakuseth, Maw of Flames :: ten damage spread across three targets on every attack.
Cityscape Leveler :: destroys a nonland permanent on cast and on every attack.
Kozilek, the Great Distortion :: refills your hand and turns dead cards into hard counterspells.
Questing Beast :: haste, deathtouch, unblockable by small creatures, and its damage cannot be prevented.

# The noncreature spells that are worth six life
Krosan Grip :: split second, so it answers the thing they were protecting.
Force of Vigor :: free on their turn, and it takes six from you only if you pay mana — cast for its alternative cost you still take the six, so use it when the two artifacts matter.
Beast Within :: any permanent, at instant speed.
Mizzium Mortars :: overloaded, a one-sided wrath since your creatures are enormous.
Brotherhood's End :: a sweeper of the small creatures that chump-block your fatties.
Calming Verse :: destroys every enchantment you do not control, and yours survive if you keep a land untapped.
Heroic Intervention :: hexproof and indestructible through a wrath.
Legolas's Quick Reflexes :: split second protection for Ruric Thar.
Pyroblast :: one mana against the blue deck holding a counterspell.
Red Elemental Blast :: the second copy.

# Closing
Pathbreaker Ibex :: trample and +X/+X to the team where X is your biggest creature. On this board it is usually lethal.
Quartzwood Crasher :: every trampling connection makes a token as big as the damage dealt.
Goreclaw, Terror of Qal Sisma :: the cheaper version of the same effect, every attack.
Beast Whisperer :: a card for every creature spell, which is nearly every card in the deck.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a mana dork. Turn-one acceleration into a turn-three or four Ruric Thar is what makes the deck's tax matter before the table has set up.
Cast your noncreature spells BEFORE Ruric Thar, not after. Deploy Rhythm of the Wild, Shadow in the Warp and the auras early; once he is out, six life per noncreature spell is a real cost even for you.
Remember he attacks every combat whether you want him to or not. Plan around it — vigilance means he still blocks, but he will be tapped for the attack trigger of whoever you sent him at.
Absorbing Man and Titania :: find it. Doubling Ruric Thar's trigger turns a slow tax into something the table cannot play through at all.
